# Template. `make init` copies this to .env, which is gitignored; it never
# overwrites an existing .env, so anything you set here is yours to keep.
#
# Compose reads .env by itself, which is the only reason this file exists: it
# interpolates `user:` in compose.yml before any container starts, and at that
# moment the Makefile's exported variables are not in play. Going through
# `make run` / `make build` sets HOST_UID/HOST_GID for you either way — the
# copy that `make init` writes carries them so that a bare `docker compose up`
# behaves the same. Adjust them if your uid/gid ever changes.

# Host ports for the two dev servers. Uncomment and change either if it clashes
# with another project's stack.
# HUGO_PORT=1313
# HUGO_RULES_PORT=1314
